Z||000002||StuGood||10-11-2000||11:00 AM||||It kind of makes sense to me.<P>If you left the headlight switch illuminated all the time so you could find it in the dark, you might tend to run down the battery.<P>What about illuminating the HL switch only when HLs are on?  IMO, because if it's too dark in there for you to find the switch, you don't have any business turning them off!  <BR>  <BR>Think the headlight switch-illumination scheme consists of the dome light, which comes on while you're getting in the car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.    <P>Or, how about glow-in-the-dark paint, for the lettering on the switch   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ?           <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-11-2000).]||||reg||12
