Z||000006||286SE'S||10-12-2000||03:40 PM||||NTSB has made regulations that automobile control switches must be illuminated at night. The headlight switch is not mentioned. They are also responsible for the elimination of push-button transmissions and a general standard of controls. So Monkeys parking brake/auto shift lever would never be found in a production vechicle. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I guess they figured that the headlight switch should be so big; how could you miss finding it? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
